          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "I focused entirely on analytic estimates. **The requested pointwise bound remains unproved.**\n\nThe strongest unconditional result obtained is\n\\[\n\\int\\chi\\mathcal L_j\\ge\n-\\frac{3-2\\sqrt2}{2}a^2\\int\\chi h_j^2,\n\\qquad \\chi=\\operatorname{sech}(a(x-x_0)).\n\\]\nThis preserves the octonionic associator’s sign, but spatial averaging prevents a pointwise conclusion.\n\nI also proved a pointwise boundary-defect bound and its complete staircase error payment. The remaining step is to bound that oriented defect by \\(E\\). An exact finite \\(E_8\\) projection now reproduces the theta source, but its auxiliary norms do not supply this missing sign.\n\nProofs, independent analytic review, and the precise next target are saved in [Note 49](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-2/active/21_quaternion_theta_geometry/notes/00_research_coordination/49_OCTONIONIC_SIGNED_BOUND_ANALYTIC_CONTINUATION_20261015.md). No numerical experiments were run."
            ]
          },
